  "swiss_army_knife": {
    "_note": "Real PyO3 ctor is SwissArmyKnife(mode, period, delta), and the param NAMES already match the Rust registry (swiss_army_knife.rs: mode/period/delta) -- no name fix needed here. The problem is 'mode': its real type is the SwissMode enum (#[pyclass(eq, eq_int)], variants EMA/SMA/Gauss/Butterworth/Smooth/HighPass/TwoPoleHighPass/BandPass/BandStop), not a plain string -- PyO3 raises TypeError(\"argument 'mode': 'str' object cannot be converted to 'SwissMode'\") if you pass the raw string 'BandPass' the registry declares as its default. A JSON-representable default (e.g. the string \"BandPass\") is not something the real constructor can accept directly, and the current metadata schema (optional_params: dict[str, JSON scalar]) has no way to express \"construct qw.SwissMode.BandPass and pass that object\" -- there's no enum-typed value representation. Deliberately NOT overriding optional_params.mode here since any JSON scalar we could put there would still fail the same round-trip; flagging as a schema gap instead of forcing a wrong fix. Callers must special-case this: cls(mode=qw.SwissMode.BandPass, period=20, delta=0.1)."
  },
